sony vaio svz finally arrived yesterday, great laptop with impeccable design and good performance, dock also arrived with the matching external graphics, but unfortunately it has its own 6.3A adapter and I don't have it, anyway spent 7 hours wiping the useless win10 and installing a dual boot win7 + debian, all very nightmarish because for the win7 to work there's only a single page (not very fast) with all the drivers, it took an ungodly amount of hours to download them all and leave the win7 operational, yes, the configuration of the external graphics card will have to wait until it's powerbrick arrives

installing debian was not much better, because although it is true that it was installed without problems, getting the sony bios to recognize the grub cost a good part of the last 3 hours, once everything is set up, all is good, and yes, it has fried batteries, aertzy keyboard, ssd bad sectors, 4GB ram, but I like it, especially if you get it complete with dock and in good condition for less than a hundred, i don't rule out burning even more on eBay on a motherboard that i've seen with the i7 and the 8GB ram, sony as always, closed the hardware reinventing every piece of common hardware for a laptop
